
# .cursor/rules/authentication-jwt.mdc

## Rule: Use Microsoft.AspNetCore.Authentication.JwtBearer
- Configure authentication middleware using the built-in JWT bearer handler.
- Do not add custom token validation logic unless asked.

## Rule: Token Handling
- Use standard claims: sub (user id), name, role, exp, iat.
- Do not expose sensitive data in JWT payload.

## Rule: Authorization Attributes
- Use [Authorize] on controllers or actions where needed.
- Do not remove or modify existing [Authorize] attributes without explicit instruction.

## Rule: Token Creation
- When generating JWTs, always include expiry (exp).
- Sign tokens using a symmetric key stored securely (e.g., via configuration or secrets manager).

## Rule: Secure Endpoints
- Do not allow anonymous access to protected endpoints unless marked with [AllowAnonymous].
